THOUGHT: NullAway complains because nameMap, superTypesCache, and implementsCache are non-null fields but not initialized in the constructor. They’re lazily initialized in methods, but NullAway requires they be definitely assigned. The safest fix is to initialize them to empty maps in the constructor; existing logic that overwrites them (e.g., in addClasspath, fillSuperTypesCache, fillImplementsCache) will still work. I’ll update the constructor accordingly and then run the NullAway build to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '37,39c\	public ClspGraph(RootNode rootNode) {
		this.root = rootNode;
		this.nameMap = new HashMap<>();
		this.superTypesCache = new HashMap<>();
		this.implementsCache = new HashMap<>();
	}
' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/clsp/ClspGraph.java && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "ClspGraph" -n new_build_output.log || true
```

